<%# ==========================================================================
  Toolbar search-term constraint chip (the removable "filter pill")
  ==========================================================================

  Renders ONLY the query (search term) constraint chip shown in the results
  toolbar, e.g.:

      [ Entire entry > women   x ]

  Facet constraints are rendered separately (see catalog/_facet_constraints).

  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHY THE `label:` LINE LOOKS THE WAY IT DOES  (read before "simplifying")
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The chip has two parts:
    * filter-name  -> the search-field label  ("Entire entry")
    * filter-value -> the typed query term     ("women")

  Stock Blacklight 9 SUPPRESSES the filter-name whenever the active search
  field is that controller's DEFAULT search field. The upstream logic lives in
  Blacklight::ConstraintsComponent#label:

      helpers.label_for_search_field(search_field) \
        unless helpers.default_search_field?(search_field)

  This app originally mirrored that guard here, which produced a visible
  regression vs. the pre-migration ("orig", BS3-era Blacklight) site:

    * BibliographyController lists "bib_keyword" (label: "Entire entry") as its
      FIRST search field and flags no field `default: true`, so bib_keyword
      becomes the default. A normal bibliography search therefore hit the
      guard and the label was dropped:

          orig:  [ Entire entry: women   x ]
          bug:   [ women                 x ]   <-- label missing

    * CatalogController (dictionary) flags "hnf" as `default: true`, and most
      dictionary searches use a NON-default field (e.g. "h"), so they dodged
      the guard and looked fine:

          [ Headword (preferred spelling only) > abacus   x ]

  The orig (pre-migration) site ALWAYS showed the search-field label in this
  chip, including for the default field. That is the blueprint we match. So we
  DROP the default-field guard and always render the label.

  This is a DOM/data difference (the label text is server-rendered), NOT a CSS
  problem -- no stylesheet can inject text the server never emitted. The caret
  separator between label and value is styled via `.filter-name::after` in
  app/assets/stylesheets and already handles this chip shape.

  NOTE: We fix it HERE (not via a Blacklight::ConstraintsComponent override)
  because THIS partial is the actual render path for the visible toolbar chip
  (rendered from catalog/_sort_and_per_page and bibliography/_sort_and_per_page).
  The full ConstraintsComponent is only used in the sidebar, where the query
  chip is CSS-hidden -- so patching the component would not affect this chip.

  TO REVERT to stock BL9 behavior, restore the guard:
      label: default_search_field?(params[:search_field]) ? nil
               : label_for_search_field(params[:search_field]),
  ========================================================================== %>
<% if search_state.query_param.present? %>
  <%= render Blacklight::ConstraintLayoutComponent.new(
        search_state: search_state,
        value: search_state.query_param,
        label: label_for_search_field(params[:search_field]),
        remove_path: search_action_path(search_state.remove_query_params),
        classes: 'query'
      ) %>
<% end %>
